      "description": "Shares one Layer across a group of Effect tests.",
      "whenToUse": "No detector replacement: use for an explicit top-level shared suite that acquires its Layer once per block; the separate timeout option carries EV014 remediation.",
      "whenNotToUse": "Do not share pure values or per-test resources; keep short-lived acquisition in each test body's inner Scope.",
      "replaces": [],
      "example": "import { layer } from \"@effect/vitest\"\nimport { Effect, Layer } from \"effect\"\nlayer(Layer.empty)(\"shared layer\", (it) => {\n  it.effect(\"uses layer\", () => Effect.void)\n})",
      "gotchas": [
        "Named blocks acquire through beforeAll and release through afterAll; hook timeout is separate from test timeout.",
        "Anonymous blocks collect their own non-skipped tasks, acquire through filtered beforeEach, register onTestFinished for last-task release, and retain afterAll cleanup fallback.",
        "Root and nested named suites accept concurrent; anonymous blocks inherit concurrency regardless of the option.",
        "Shared TestClock/TestConsole and resource context are cached per block; each Effect test still gets a fresh Scope.",
        "Nested layers fork the parent memo map; excludeTestServices propagates and nested signatures expose concurrent/timeout only.",
        "Layer cleanup intentionally runs without the last test aborted signal. Hooks and body finalizers have different timeout ownership."
      ]
    },
