        "D5 reserves canonical utils helpers for Option, Result, and Exit while ordinary values may use expect."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "readme.exit",
      "name": "README:Testing Successes and Failures as `Exit`",
      "kind": "readme-section",
      "file": "packages/vitest/README.md",
      "startLine": 114,
      "endLine": 145,
      "signature": "Testing Successes and Failures as `Exit`",
      "description": "Capturing both Effect success and failure as Exit",
      "whenToUse": "Use for result-outcome-assertion findings (EV005, candidate class result-outcome-assertion) with unresolved, mixed or assertion-only outcomes. Review Effect.result to Effect.exit migration while preserving matcher polarity and existing operands: Result failure holds an error, whereas Exit failure holds a Cause. Select a specific Exit helper only when its expected value or Cause is established; never invent one from a Boolean predicate or partial error field.",
      "whenNotToUse": "Do not hand-compare Exit tags or use Result helpers on an Exit.",
      "replaces": ["EV005"],
      "example": "import { assertExitSuccess } from \"@effect/vitest/utils\"\nimport { Effect } from \"effect\"\nconst program = Effect.exit(Effect.succeed(2)).pipe(Effect.tap((exit) => Effect.sync(() => assertExitSuccess(exit, 2))))\nvoid program",
      "gotchas": [
        "The README predates the repository D5 helper rule; use assertExitSuccess or assertExitFailure."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "readme.testclock",
      "name": "README:Using the TestClock",
      "kind": "readme-section",
      "file": "packages/vitest/README.md",
      "startLine": 146,
      "endLine": 192,
      "signature": "Using the TestClock",
      "description": "Deterministic time control with TestClock adjustment",
      "whenToUse": "Use for test-clock-stall-risk findings (EV008, candidate class test-clock-stall-risk) by coordinating scheduled work with TestClock advancement in the same effect test. Diagnose the root cause first (D6). Only a bounded external-system wait that actually requires live time should use the TestClock.withLive alternative; wrap that wait and its timeout without replacing the surrounding test clock.",
      "whenNotToUse": "Do not switch a sleeping test to live time solely to avoid driving TestClock.",
      "replaces": ["EV008"],
      "example": "import { it } from \"@effect/vitest\"\nimport * as TestClock from \"effect/testing/TestClock\"\nit.effect(\"clock\", () => TestClock.adjust(\"1 second\"))",
      "gotchas": [
        "Import TestClock from effect/testing/TestClock at the pin.",
        "Fork scheduled work before adjusting when concurrency is required.",
        "it.layer shares TestClock state across its block; this README section only documents per-test it.effect."
      ]
    },
    {
